{"code":200,"message":"OK","tweet":{"url":"https://x.com/MozeTech/status/2102913506815471882","id":"2102913506815471882","text":"Opus 5.5 just one-shot this entire pixel-art game. Oh, and the prompt? It was barely three sentences. I gave claude creative license to make whatever game it wanted to, and oh boy did it cook\n\nThe capabilities of this model are genuinely ridiculous, I fed GPT Sol-6 the same prompt and the results were shockingly poor. Seems like Sol-6 is taking the Opus 5 role this time around.\n\nWith models becoming this good, I'm struggling to see the need to purchase games anymore. If you can have any game you want created in a single prompt, with beautiful art, story, etc - what's the point of sinking $60+? \n\nLol, obviously because the stories and ideas that humans have are still way better than whatever these models can still do. However, the gaming industry is definitely going to be shaken now - excited to see what's gonna come out of this!\n\nAnyway, here's a side by side comparison of both outputs, thoughts?\n\nAlso if you wanted to play it yourself:\nhttps://skerry-light.vercel.app/\n\nLeft is Claude, right is Opus","raw_text":{"text":"Opus 5.5 just one-shot this entire pixel-art game. Oh, and the prompt? It was barely three sentences. I gave claude creative license to make whatever game it wanted to, and oh boy did it cook\n\nThe capabilities of this model are genuinely ridiculous, I fed GPT Sol-6 the same prompt and the results were shockingly poor. Seems like Sol-6 is taking the Opus 5 role this time around.\n\nWith models becoming this good, I'm struggling to see the need to purchase games anymore. If you can have any game you want created in a single prompt, with beautiful art, story, etc - what's the point of sinking $60+? \n\nLol, obviously because the stories and ideas that humans have are still way better than whatever these models can still do. However, the gaming industry is definitely going to be shaken now - excited to see what's gonna come out of this!\n\nAnyway, here's a side by side comparison of both outputs, thoughts?\n\nAlso if you wanted to play it yourself:\nhttps://t.co/qR4IarR4hX\n\nLeft is Claude, right is Opus","display_text_range":[0,1005],"facets":[{"type":"media","indices":[275,298],"id":"2102906771933442048","display":"pic.x.com/IRjR3BvjGJ","original":"https://t.co/IRjR3BvjGJ","replacement":"https://x.com/MozeTech/status/2102913506815471882/video/1"},{"type":"media","indices":[275,298],"id":"2102908409196814336","display":"pic.x.com/IRjR3BvjGJ","original":"https://t.co/IRjR3BvjGJ","replacement":"https://x.com/MozeTech/status/2102913506815471882/video/1"},{"type":"url","indices":[951,974],"original":"https://t.co/qR4IarR4hX","replacement":"https://skerry-light.vercel.app/","display":"skerry-light.vercel.app"}]},"author":{"screen_name":"MozeTech","url":"https://x.com/MozeTech","id":"1979773990219685888","followers":277,"following":272,"likes":1078,"media_count":115,"name":"Max","description":"i like making mini games\nai video production\nphilosophize every now and then\ni love hacking algorithms while being non-technical\ndesign and aesthetics lover","raw_description":{"text":"i like making mini games\nai video production\nphilosophize every now and then\ni love hacking algorithms while being non-technical\ndesign and aesthetics lover","facets":[]},"location":"San Francisco","banner_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1979773990219685888/1761442168","avatar_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1979775641290526720/3f4mW1_y_200x200.jpg","joined":"Sun Oct 19 04:58:23 +0000 2025","protected":false,"website":null,"verification":{"verified":true,"verified_at":null,"type":"individual"},"avatar_color":null},"replies":1,"retweets":1,"likes":7,"bookmarks":1,"quotes":0,"created_at":"Thu Sep 24 00:10:24 +0000 2026","created_timestamp":1790208624,"possibly_sensitive":false,"views":516,"is_note_tweet":true,"community_note":null,"lang":"en","replying_to":null,"replying_to_stat